window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-2d083870d670ea3a"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"work-with-agents-in-space\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"space\">在 Space 中与智能体协作</h1> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在页面 URL 后追加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取文档的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>在 Space 页面中，你可以与 ChatGPT 或 dot 一起起草、研究或修改内容。可用智能体和已连接工具取决于你的访问权限。</p> <blockquote> <p>插图：输入 @ 后打开的页面提及菜单，其中有“全部”“人员”“页面”和“聊天”标签页；可选择 ChatGPT 开始任务，也可选择 My dot 向你的 dot 发送提示词。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"start-with-a-bounded-request\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"choose-how-to-ask-for-help\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_1\">选择求助方式</h2> <p>如果问题需要讨论、制定计划或修改内容，可以在页面旁边的对话中提出。只需小幅修改时，可以选择相关文字，在行内请 ChatGPT 或 dot 帮忙，也可以添加评论。你能看到哪些控制项取决于自己的访问权限。</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>你的目标</th> <th>在哪里提出请求</th> <th>需要检查什么</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>探索问题或讨论较大的修改。</td> <td>在页面旁边的对话中提出。说明你希望只在聊天中获得回答，还是要编辑页面。</td> <td>对话内容以及你要求对页面所作的修改。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>重写选中的文字。</td> <td>选中文字，并在提供该选项时选择 <strong>Ask for change（提出修改）</strong>。</td> <td>接受修改前，先检查建议的内容。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>直接在页面中请 ChatGPT 或 dot 帮忙。</td> <td>输入 <code>@ChatGPT</code> 或 <code>@dot</code>，然后在行内输入提示词。</td> <td>回复内容以及对页面所作的任何修改。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>在评论讨论中提出具体请求。</td> <td>输入 <code>@ChatGPT</code> 或 <code>@dot</code>，并在后面写明请求。</td> <td>回复内容以及对页面所作的任何修改。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>提及 ChatGPT 或 dot 就是在请相应的智能体执行你的请求。给其他人的评论则是反馈。发送之前，请确认接收对象。</p> <blockquote> <p>插图：团队外出活动计划中选中的句子旁有一条评论，提及 @ChatGPT 并要求更改开始日期。评论中显示作者和时间戳，下方是空白的回复编辑框。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"use-slash-commands\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">使用斜杠命令</h2> <p>在页面中输入 <code>/</code> 可打开斜杠菜单。选择 <strong>Generate（生成）</strong> 可在行内生成文字，选择 <strong>Visualize（可视化）</strong> 可创建交互式可视化内容，选择 <strong>Image（图像）</strong> 可添加图像区块。在图像区块中，选择 <strong>Generate（生成）</strong> 并描述你希望生成的图像。更多示例请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-c7393fbab700d02d?anchor=add-content-with-the-insert-menu\">向页面添加内容</a>和<a href=\"#/article/a-c7393fbab700d02d?anchor=generate-images\">生成图像</a>。</p> <blockquote> <p>插图：输入 / 后出现的页面斜杠菜单，其中可选择 Generate 来描述要撰写的内容、Visualize 来创建可视化内容，以及 Image 来上传或生成图像。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"use-dots-in-space\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"space-dots\">在 Space 中使用 dots</h2> <p>你可以直接在 ChatGPT Space 中与 <a href=\"#/article/a-1323ad8861010e1b\">dots</a> 协作。在页面中输入 <code>@</code> 可打开提及菜单，然后选择你的 dot。</p> <p>在行内或页面评论中输入 <code>@dot</code>，再写上提示词。例如：</p>  <p>继续之前，请检查 dot 的回复以及它对页面作出的任何修改。</p> <p><a id=\"revise-a-launch-brief\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">修改发布简报</h2> <p>如果简报提到了发布日期，而所链接的计划显示该日期仍待批准，请先检查来源，然后选择相应句子，并在提供该选项时选择 <strong>Ask for change（提出修改）</strong>：</p> <blockquote> <p>请将日期说明为“拟定日期，尚待批准”。保留日期和来源链接不变。</p> </blockquote> <p>接受修改建议前，请先检查措辞。</p> <p><a id=\"verify-recurring-work-separately\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">单独验证定期任务</h2> <p>功能 <strong>Keep Updated（保持更新）</strong> 在发布初期尚不可用。</p> <p>要设置定期工作，请在聊天中向 ChatGPT 提出请求，并检查已保存的计划。仅在页面或其说明中写明执行频率，并不能确认任务已经排期。</p> <p>设置完成后，请检查已保存的任务、执行时间和启用状态；然后检查它是否实际运行，以及页面是否因此更新。具体控制项取决于你的账户中可用的功能。</p> <p>有关计划管理和执行要求，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-b5406e60cbfa0b68\">计划任务</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"work-with-others\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">与他人协作</h2> <p>协作者可以共享页面内容，但可能使用不同的智能体、已连接工具或说明。请事先商定各自负责修改什么，并共同检查结果。</p> <p>有关访问和审阅，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-418e376165928c0b\">在 Space 中协作</a>。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"work-with-agents-in-space\">Work with agents in Space</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Work with ChatGPT or a dot in Space to draft, research, or revise a page. Available agents and connected tools depend on your access.</p> <blockquote> <p>Illustration: The page mention menu after typing @, with All, People, Pages, and Chats tabs, ChatGPT to start a task, and My dot to send a prompt to your dot.</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"start-with-a-bounded-request\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"choose-how-to-ask-for-help\">Choose how to ask for help</h2> <p>Use the conversation alongside a page for questions, planning, or a revision that needs discussion. For a small change, select the relevant text, ask ChatGPT or a dot inline, or add a comment. The controls offered depend on your access.</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Your goal</th> <th>Where to ask</th> <th>What to review</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Explore a question or discuss a larger revision.</td> <td>The conversation alongside the page. State whether to answer in chat or edit the page.</td> <td>The conversation and any requested page edits.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Rewrite selected text.</td> <td>Select the text and use <strong>Ask for change</strong>, when offered.</td> <td>The proposed edit before accepting it.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Ask ChatGPT or a dot directly in the page.</td> <td>Type <code>@ChatGPT</code> or <code>@dot</code> followed by your prompt inline.</td> <td>The reply and any changes to the page.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Keep a specific request in a comment discussion.</td> <td>Mention <code>@ChatGPT</code> or <code>@dot</code> followed by your prompt.</td> <td>The reply and any changes to the page.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>Mentioning ChatGPT or a dot asks that agent to act on your request. A comment to another person leaves feedback for them. Check the recipient before sending.</p> <blockquote> <p>Illustration: A selected sentence in an offsite plan has a comment mentioning @ChatGPT to change its start date. The comment includes the author, timestamp, and an empty Reply composer.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"use-slash-commands\">Use slash commands</h2> <p>Type <code>/</code> in a page to open the slash menu. Choose <strong>Generate</strong> to generate text inline, <strong>Visualize</strong> to create an interactive visualization, or <strong>Image</strong> to add an image block. In the image block, choose <strong>Generate</strong> and describe the image you want. See <a href=\"#/article/a-c7393fbab700d02d?anchor=add-content-with-the-insert-menu\">Add content to a page</a> and <a href=\"#/article/a-c7393fbab700d02d?anchor=generate-images\">Generate images</a> for more examples.</p> <blockquote> <p>Illustration: The page slash menu after typing /, with Generate to describe what you want to write, Visualize to create an interactive visualization, and Image to upload or generate an image.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"use-dots-in-space\">Use dots in Space</h2> <p>You can work with <a href=\"#/article/a-1323ad8861010e1b\">dots</a> directly in ChatGPT Space. Type <code>@</code> in a page to open the mention menu and choose your dot.</p> <p>Type <code>@dot</code> followed by your prompt inline or in a page comment. For example:</p>  <p>Review your dot's reply and any changes to the page before continuing.</p> <h2 id=\"revise-a-launch-brief\">Revise a launch brief</h2> <p>If a brief names a launch date but the linked plan says it still needs approval, check the source, then select the sentence and use <strong>Ask for change</strong>, when offered:</p> <blockquote> <p>Describe the date as proposed and awaiting approval. Keep the date and source link unchanged.</p> </blockquote> <p>Review the proposed wording before accepting it.</p> <h2 id=\"verify-recurring-work-separately\">Verify recurring work separately</h2> <p>Keep Updated isn’t available at launch.</p> <p>To set up recurring work, ask ChatGPT in chat and review the saved schedule. Writing a cadence in a page or its instructions doesn't by itself confirm that a task is scheduled.</p> <p>After setup, review the saved task, its timing, and whether it's enabled. Then check an actual run and the resulting page update. These controls depend on what's available in your account.</p> <p>For schedule management and execution requirements, see <a href=\"#/article/a-b5406e60cbfa0b68\">Scheduled tasks</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"work-with-others\">Work with others</h2> <p>Collaborators share the page content, but may use different agents, connected tools, or instructions. Agree on who is changing what and review the result.</p> <p>See <a href=\"#/article/a-418e376165928c0b\">Collaboration</a> for access and review guidance.</p>"};
